  "description": "The general election for California's 43rd Congressional District pits 18-term incumbent Democrat Maxine Waters against Republican challenger Cristian Morales. Waters, first elected in 1990 and the oldest Democrat in Congress at age 87, has represented the district (reconfigured through redistricting) for decades and currently serves as Ranking Member on the House Financial Services Committee. The district, which includes portions of South Los Angeles and the South Bay region such as Inglewood, Hawthorne, Gardena, Compton, and Torrance, is heavily Democratic (57.89% of registered voters) and rated 'Solid D' by the Cook Political Report. The top-two primary on June 2, 2026, advanced Waters (63.8%) and Morales (16.9%) to the general election, with two other Democratic candidates eliminated.",
